  "steps": [
    "Combine all the burger ingredients except the oil in a bowl, breaking up the turkey with a fork, then knead gently with a wet hand until mixed. The mixture will be soft. With damp hands, shape into 3 or 4 patties and refrigerate until ready to cook.",
    "Toss the slaw ingredients together and set aside. Mix the mayonnaise and sriracha for the aioli.",
    "Preheat a grill to medium and brush the grates with the oil. Grill the burgers until golden and 165°F in the center, 5 to 6 minutes per side.",
    "Toast the buns on the grill. Spread aioli on the bottom buns and top with the patties, slaw, more aioli, and the top buns."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Feasting At Home pulls the patties at 160°F and lets carryover heat finish them; ground turkey is safe at 165°F, so check the center before serving.",
    "To pan-sear instead, cook the patties in an oiled skillet over medium heat for the same time.",
    "The slaw can be made a day ahead and the aioli up to 3 days ahead."
  ],
